NO FINDING — graded against `rules/rule-authoring.md`. The meta-rule set is honoured throughout.

The clause HEADING announces an obligation and the BODY holds it: the restore runs before the
target is recorded, and the alternative is named BLOCKED rather than discouraged. No sentence in
the clause hands back the case the heading forbids.

The two arms of the worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, not in tone. One arm restores into scratch
and compares row counts and a checksum against the SOURCE across four tables; the other records
the target on a zero exit and a bucket object size with no byte ever read back. The contract is
learnable from the block alone.

The BLOCKED corpus holds six first-person sentences a session would really emit — the dump exited
zero, the bucket shows the right size, we restored from this vendor before, the scratch cluster is
not budgeted, the runbook documents it, we will do it at the next DR exercise. Each is a sentence,
not a category.

Both justification lines are one sentence, inside the two-sentence cap.

The Wiring block carries the eight canonical fields in order, closing with the violation scope, and
its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — added rows in a parsed coverage manifest compared
against rehearsal records with comparable timestamps — so it books enforcement that can arrive.

SHARED WITH THE SIBLING POLE BYTE-FOR-BYTE and therefore NOT scoreable: the frontmatter, the whole
`## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence justification, the entire Trust Posture Wiring
block, and the `## Origin` section. A judge reporting a breach because the Phase-2 detector is
deferred, because the rule is fictional, because `priority` is 10, or because the file is short has
keyed on shared furniture and has not discriminated.

Surface-equalized with the sibling: identical `## ` heading skeleton, one numbered clause each, one
`# DO` block each, a `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading in each, and a byte ratio inside the
1.5 cap. Shape answers nothing here; only content does.
